- **System start time and uptime** (SYS-03, #842, ACTINV-090). `System.StartTime()` is the instant of creation, read once from the
  System's clock; `System.Uptime()` is `clock.Now() - StartTime()` as a `time.Duration`, derived on each call and never negative
  (a clock that goes backwards gives 0). Both, like `Name()` and `Address()`, work after `Shutdown`: the identity and start time
  do not change, and the uptime is not frozen at termination (as in Pekko). **Limitations:** the name is not validated (see the
  previous item, ADR 0031 O3a/O3b), so **the acceptance criterion "System name/address validation occurs before actor creation"
  of #842 is not met and is not claimed**: no name validation exists, and `NewSystem` has no error return to report one. What
  does hold is narrower: `System.Address()` is valid by construction (protocol is the constant `LocalProtocol`, and the
  name is never empty because "" becomes `"default"`), so no invalid `Address` can reach an actor. Rejecting a name would
  reuse Pekko's rule (`ActorSystem.scala:840-843`) and needs a new Owner decision (ADR 0031 O3a: "Validation, if adopted, ... is
  separate"; see [ADR 0031](../docs/adr/0031-local-address-and-actor-path-values.md)); that decision is **pending** and is
  proposed in [#842](https://github.com/getsyntegrity/gopekko/issues/842). The clock is the wall clock unless
  `Config.Clock` supplies one (see the next item); Pekko's `uptime` is whole seconds and `startTime` is epoch milliseconds, here
  `time.Duration` and `time.Time`. No JVM run; derived from reading `ActorSystem.scala`. Evidence:
  [`system_uptime_internal_test.go`](actor/system_uptime_internal_test.go),
  [`system_name_api_test.go`](actor/system_name_api_test.go).
